<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Ash'karr plant names. Owner 2026-09-05, on the plant register's rename-gap
       finding: the campaign had renamed 12 vanilla plants and left the rest under
       Earth names, so roses and dandelions were growing on a desert world.

       Coined in CLADES so related flora share a morpheme and the ecosystem reads
       as evolved rather than assembled - the same convention as
       CreatureNames_Ashkarr.xml:
         -skal   dry bladed groundcover (grasses)
         sarn-   standing-water plants (only legal in the water-high biomes)
         -vaesh  flowering plants
         grell   scrub and thorn
         maw     carrion blooms

       Left ALONE deliberately: plants whose vanilla names are already invented
       (healroot, devilstrand, psychoid, smokeleaf, glowstool, timbershroom,
       chokevine, witchwood, agarilux ...) - renaming those would churn without
       gain and break player recognition.

       🔴 LABEL ONLY. No defName is touched. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Plant_Grass"]/label</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Plant_Grass"]/label</xpath>
      <value><label>duneskal</label></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>   <!-- was "grass" -->

